cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  picchain: an agent-drivable design, simulation and verification chain for
  photonic integrated circuits
message: "If this software is used in work that is published, please cite it."
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<OWNER>/<REPO>"
abstract: >-
  A headless design chain for photonic integrated circuits. A design is
  expressed as a single YAML file carrying its own acceptance criteria; the
  chain returns a JSON metric tree and a non-zero exit code where those criteria
  are unmet. Seventeen stages take a device from cross-section to a
  rule-checked mask and a submission manifest, assembled from open tools. It is
  validated against a published and measured thin-film lithium niobate
  extended-DBR Pockels laser, and the agreements and disagreements with that
  device are recorded rather than reconciled.
keywords:
  - photonics
  - photonic integrated circuits
  - thin-film lithium niobate
  - electronic design automation
  - Bragg grating
  - coupled-mode theory
authors:
  - family-names: Leow
    given-names: "Kwang Siong Jeremy"
  - name: "Republic of Singapore"

# The repository URL above remains a placeholder. Set it to the published
